293
00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:12.540
If you look at government interventions, they usually don't work very well.

294
00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:19.700
If the government backs away, is smaller, less impactful, is actually is a far better thing.

295
00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:27.320
So if you look at Argentina as a case study, there's a famous video that went viral of Malay ripping things off the board, all the government agencies.

296
00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:30.620
And now you can see that they have a surplus.

297
00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.540
Inflation is declining.

298
00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:38.420
And then he stopped regulation of the rental market, the housing market.

299
00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:41.520
And now there is an abundance of supply.

300
00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:46.920
So all they had to do is get out of the way and the market will solve a lot of these problems.

301
00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:54.840
So the question is really what value does the government add if they are in the mix?

302
00:18:54.940 --> 00:19:03.900
And I think it's a negative value in many cases because you're electing people that are not necessarily experts at what they're supposed to be managing.

303
00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:18.040
So I think having the government removed from many things, especially money, money supply, money management is a big benefit because it corrupts the whole system in the end.

304
00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:23.780
Like in Canada, the Central Bank of Canada, Bank of Canada is effectively the ATM for the government.

305
00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:27.660
