374
00:23:16.640 --> 00:23:18.480
They never boost the limits, right?

375
00:23:18.860 --> 00:23:22.620
There's the $10,000 limit for moving cash across borders.

376
00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:29.620
But if you go back in time when that law was first passed, the real value of that money back then was like $80,000.

377
00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:30.140
Wow.

378
00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:31.400
But the number doesn't change.

379
00:23:31.540 --> 00:23:31.660
Yeah.

380
00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:36.940
So eventually, you'll only be able to bring enough money across the border to eat, right?

381
00:23:37.120 --> 00:23:37.820
That is insane.

382
00:23:37.960 --> 00:23:38.960
Yeah, that's a good point.

383
00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:48.040
But yeah, like all of these numbers, the system is broken because they're fixed on these numbers that are getting more worthless all the time.

384
00:23:48.520 --> 00:23:52.700
And the reason it's getting more worthless is because, one, you're printing more of it.

385
00:23:52.880 --> 00:23:57.580
But two, you're eliminating a key property of money, which is it has to free flow.

386
00:23:57.580 --> 00:24:06.820
So if you look at growing economies where people invest, they invest in places where they can move money in and out easily.

387
00:24:07.280 --> 00:24:14.660
Nobody wants to invest in a place where there's a big door in and a small door out because there's risk.

388
00:24:14.980 --> 00:24:16.140
There's political risk.

389
00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:20.800
There's many reasons you want to be able to move capital in and out quickly.

390
00:24:21.360 --> 00:24:27.780
And the growth that we've seen in Asia in the past, I think, is from free flow of capital.

391
00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:36.780
And as countries develop, they kind of dial it back and go into a protectionism mode and try to keep what they have.

392
00:24:36.860 --> 00:24:42.540
And they don't realize that not having money moving easily is a detriment.

393
00:24:42.940 --> 00:24:45.860
But I think that gives opportunity to other countries in the world.

394
00:24:45.860 --> 00:24:49.860
If you look at Latin America, you can see they're embracing money.

395
00:24:50.620 --> 00:24:51.160
They want money.

396
